## Why This Is Asked
This question probes the ability to design production-grade evaluation for hallucination, faithfulness, and relevance in a real-world, cross-brand setting with versioned corpora and latency constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Grounding fidelity: mapping claims to exact doc versions with timestamps
- Hallucination detection: counterfactual prompts, calibration
- Citation drift: monitoring updates across corpus versions
- Latency constraints: streaming vs batch, budgets, backpressure
- Multilingual/multimodal: image/text handling, alignment
- Observability: metrics, dashboards, SLAs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal skeleton showing core steps
function evalRun(input, version) {
  const claims = extractClaims(input);
  const grounded = ground(claims, version);
  const halluc = detectHallucinations(grounded);
  const drift = computeDrift(versionHistory, grounded);
  return {
    grounding: grounded.metrics,
    hallucination: halluc.metrics,
    drift: drift.score,
    latency: measureLatency()
  };
}
```

